# Paths are relative to the REPO ROOT — that is the build context (see Dockerfile).
#
# node_modules is the load-bearing entry: without it the host's tree (built against the host's
# platform) is copied into the builder stage and shadows the one `npm ci` just resolved for linux.
# The failure is not a missing module but a native binary for the wrong OS, which surfaces as an
# opaque runtime error rather than a build error.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/coverage
**/results.xml

**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log

# Other components of the monorepo. The build only ever COPYs apps/aigateway-ui, so shipping the
# rest of the repo to the daemon is pure transfer cost.
apps/aigateway
apps/scoreboard
apps/screamingface-engine
packages
docs
.docs
.claude
